- Event column: progression_event (1 = event occurred, 0 = censored)
- Covariates: gene_score (categorical with levels: low, medium, high), age (continuous), sex (binary)
- Set gene_score reference level to "low" using pd.Categorical with categories=['low','medium','high']
- Use CoxPHFitter from lifelines to fit the model
- Extract hazard ratios (exp(coef)), 95% confidence intervals (exp(coef lower 95%, exp(coef upper 95%)), and p-values for the gene_score contrasts only (gene_score_medium vs low, gene_score_high vs low)
- Create a DataFrame with columns: Gene_Score, Hazard_Ratio, CI_Lower_95, CI_Upper_95, P_value
  - Gene_Score values should be "medium_vs_low" and "high_vs_low"
  - Round numeric values to 4 decimal places for readability but keep full precision in the CSV
- Save to /mnt/data/lengyang/youjia_project/autoba/BABench/src/promptbio-bench/tasks/b-9-2/result_79/toolsgenie_20260709/data/cox_regression_results.csv
